Start();
include(utilities);
include(unitTests);
registry(fILEs);
define
    kantGrammar File='incant/kantGrammar';
    ;
include(kantGrammar);
search reset stack KantGrammar Grokking;
search Utilities UnitTests;
registry(NotBuiltT);
define
    qa=2;
    qb=3;
    qr=0;
    it1;
    nbAct code={ qr = qa | qb; print 6:; };
    nbN code={
        qr = qa | qb;
        print 6:;
        };
    nlReqN owner source result rule;
    nbNew code={
        nlSrc := argument.CodE;
        nlReqN.owner  := argument;
        nlReqN.source := nlSrc;
        nlReqN.rule   := KantGrammar["STARt"];
        if compileIn(nlReqN);
            nlBlock = nlReqN.result;
            *nlBlock :. noPrinT;
            argument :. isActioN;
            argument +< *nlBlock;
        };
    ;
search NotBuiltT Utilities UnitTests list;
stop();

notBuiltT -- SEQ 599 A0 (Tony, 2026-11-10): the ten Operators entries that had no method (| ^ GO ? >> << :> :< :- &) are
RESERVED. Each is bound to one shared method, opNotBuilt, and using one between two operands refuses by name on both
roads, "REFUSED <op> -- is not built yet -- a reserved operator (SEQ 599)", and the statement does nothing. In a prefix
position they refuse with the prefix wording, as every operator that is not a unary does (prefixOpT pins that). When one
is built for real its refusal is replaced by its method (| is ruled as x | f meaning f(x), not scheduled).

Not run alone: pop.sh appends the row's statements, print "Q", a sentinel; one process per run. Each value reads:
[stdout, lines joined by |] nb<lines with the not-built wording naming this row's op> o<other REFUSED lines> x<exit>
s<sentinel>.

OPS: one line per reserved operator. pop.sh runs each as qr = qa <op> qb; print qr:; print 7:; at top level (old road)
and as it1 = FILe("qr = qa <op> qb; print qr:;"); print 7:; (new road). Intended on the old road [0 |7 |Q |] nb1 o0 x0 s1
(qr keeps its 0 and the next statement runs); on the new road [7 |Q |] nb1 o0 x0 s1 (an engine refusal ends the FILe
call's unit; the statement after the call runs). Fields are separated by TABS (operators use | and ^).

ROWS, separated by TABS -- id, statements, op named in the refusal, value today (seal 432's binary), intended:
NB-C1 / NB-C2  a reserved operator as an if's condition, old road and new: neither arm runs.
NB-A1          an old-road action, interpreted: refused, the action ends there (6 is not printed).
NB-A2          the same action compiled (testing()).
NB-A3          a new-road action body.

